# PATENT CLAIMS

## Claim 1 (Independent - System Claim)

A system for negotiating Multimedia Broadcast Multicast Service (MBMS) capability exposure in a telecommunications network, the system comprising:

a third-party application server configured to:
- generate a capability exposure request comprising at least one MBMS service parameter, a target service area identifier, and an application-layer quality-of-service requirement;
- transmit the capability exposure request to a Service Capability Exposure Function (SCEF);

the SCEF communicatively coupled to the third-party application server, the SCEF configured to:
- receive the capability exposure request from the third-party application server;
- translate the capability exposure request into a network-layer capability query compatible with a Home Subscriber Server (HSS) interface protocol;
- transmit the network-layer capability query to a Home Subscriber Server (HSS);

the HSS communicatively coupled to the SCEF, the HSS configured to:
- receive the network-layer capability query;
- determine, based on subscriber profile data and network policy data, whether the requested MBMS capability is authorized for exposure to the third-party application server;
- forward, upon determination of authorization, an MBMS resource allocation request to a Broadcast Multicast Service Center (BM-SC);

the BM-SC communicatively coupled to the HSS, the BM-SC configured to:
- receive the MBMS resource allocation request;
- determine availability of MBMS bearer resources within the target service area;
- generate a capability exposure response comprising at least one of an allocated bearer identifier, a session start time, and a maximum bit rate; and
- transmit the capability exposure response to the HSS for forwarding, via the SCEF, to the third-party application server,

wherein the SCEF is further configured to translate the capability exposure response into an application-layer format compatible with the third-party application server prior to delivery.

---

## Claim 2 (Dependent)

The system of claim 1, wherein the capability exposure request further comprises a temporal validity window, and wherein the SCEF is further configured to reject the capability exposure request without forwarding it to the HSS if the temporal validity window falls outside a predetermined exposure policy interval maintained at the SCEF.

## Claim 3 (Dependent)

The system of claim 1, wherein the HSS is further configured to negotiate, with the BM-SC, a modified set of MBMS parameters differing from the at least one MBMS service parameter of the capability exposure request when the BM-SC indicates that the originally requested parameters exceed available network resources, and wherein the SCEF is further configured to relay the modified set of MBMS parameters to the third-party application server as a counter-offer.

## Claim 4 (Dependent)

The system of claim 3, wherein the third-party application server is further configured to transmit an acceptance or rejection of the counter-offer to the SCEF, and wherein the BM-SC allocates MBMS bearer resources only upon receipt, via the HSS and the SCEF, of an acceptance of the counter-offer.

## Claim 5 (Dependent)

The system of claim 1, wherein the HSS determines whether the requested MBMS capability is authorized by verifying a service level agreement identifier included in the capability exposure request against a stored authorization record associated with the third-party application server.

## Claim 6 (Dependent)

The system of claim 1, wherein the SCEF is further configured to monitor a plurality of capability exposure requests from a plurality of third-party application servers and to apply a rate-limiting policy to the network-layer capability query transmitted to the HSS.

## Claim 7 (Dependent)

The system of claim 1, wherein the at least one MBMS service parameter comprises at least one of: a content type identifier, a geographic broadcast area, a broadcast start time, a broadcast duration, and a required quality-of-service class.

## Claim 8 (Dependent)

The system of claim 1, wherein the BM-SC is further configured to reserve the allocated bearer identifier for a predetermined guard period prior to session start time, and to release the allocated bearer identifier if a session activation message is not received from the third-party application server via the SCEF and the HSS within the guard period.

---

## Claim 9 (Independent - Method Claim)

A method for negotiating Multimedia Broadcast Multicast Service (MBMS) capability exposure in a telecommunications network, the method comprising:

receiving, at a Service Capability Exposure Function (SCEF), a capability exposure request from a third-party application server, the capability exposure request comprising at least one MBMS service parameter and a target service area identifier;

translating, by the SCEF, the capability exposure request into a network-layer capability query;

transmitting the network-layer capability query to a Home Subscriber Server (HSS);

determining, at the HSS, based on subscriber profile data, whether the requested MBMS capability is authorized for exposure;

responsive to determining authorization, transmitting an MBMS resource allocation request from the HSS to a Broadcast Multicast Service Center (BM-SC);

evaluating, at the BM-SC, availability of MBMS bearer resources within the target service area;

generating, at the BM-SC, a capability exposure response comprising an allocated bearer identifier and a maximum bit rate;

transmitting the capability exposure response from the BM-SC to the HSS;

forwarding the capability exposure response from the HSS to the SCEF; and

translating, by the SCEF, the capability exposure response into an application-layer format and delivering the translated capability exposure response to the third-party application server.

## Claim 10 (Dependent)

The method of claim 9, further comprising:

determining, at the BM-SC, that the at least one MBMS service parameter exceeds an available network resource threshold;

generating, at the BM-SC, a modified MBMS parameter set;

transmitting the modified MBMS parameter set to the third-party application server via the HSS and the SCEF as a counter-offer; and

allocating MBMS bearer resources at the BM-SC only upon receipt of an acceptance of the counter-offer from the third-party application server.

## Claim 11 (Dependent)

The method of claim 9, further comprising rejecting, at the SCEF, the capability exposure request without forwarding the network-layer capability query to the HSS, upon determining that the capability exposure request violates a predetermined exposure policy stored at the SCEF.

---

## Claim 12 (Independent - Non-Transitory Computer-Readable Medium Claim)

A non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that, when executed by one or more processors of a Service Capability Exposure Function (SCEF), cause the SCEF to perform operations comprising:

receiving a capability exposure request from a third-party application server, the capability exposure request comprising at least one MBMS service parameter;

authenticating the third-party application server based on a credential included in the capability exposure request;

translating the capability exposure request into a network-layer capability query compatible with a Home Subscriber Server (HSS);

transmitting the network-layer capability query to the HSS for authorization determination and subsequent forwarding to a Broadcast Multicast Service Center (BM-SC) for resource negotiation;

receiving, from the HSS, a capability exposure response reflecting an outcome of resource negotiation between the HSS and the BM-SC; and

translating the capability exposure response into an application-layer format for delivery to the third-party application server.

## Claim 13 (Dependent)

The non-transitory computer-readable medium of claim 12, wherein the operations further comprise storing, at the SCEF, a mapping between the capability exposure request and a transaction identifier, and correlating the capability exposure response received from the HSS with the capability exposure request using the transaction identifier.
